     The ooppeennppaamm__rreeaaddlliinnee() function reads a line from a file, and returns it
     in a NUL-terminated buffer allocated with malloc(3).

     The ooppeennppaamm__rreeaaddlliinnee() function performs a certain amount of processing
     on the data it reads:

     ••   Comments (introduced by a hash sign) are stripped.

     ••   Blank lines are ignored.

     ••   If a line ends in a backslash, the backslash is stripped and the next
         line is appended.

     If _l_i_n_e_n_o is not NULL, the integer variable it points to is incremented
     every time a newline character is read.

     If _l_e_n_p is not NULL, the length of the line (not including the terminat‐
     ing NUL character) is stored in the variable it points to.

     The caller is responsible for releasing the returned buffer by passing it
     to free(3).

